Find returns filepath.WalkDir's result; the callback returns its err argument,
fs.SkipDir or walk.ErrTooMany. Expected: sentinel walk.ErrTooMany through the dynamic
call of the callback inside filepath, plus WalkDir's own os.Lstat/ReadDir errors
(some marked possibly handled by WalkDir's SkipDir/SkipAll comparisons).
fs.SkipDir and fs.SkipAll must NOT appear: WalkDir turns them into nil.
-- args --
walk/walk.go:@find
